From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Akhil R <akhilrajeev@nvidia.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Aug 2024 10:37:13 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 035/140] NVIDIA: SAUCE: i2c: tegra: resume explicitly if
 pm_runtime is disabled

This is a WAR to handle NOIRQ suspend/resume in I2C client devices.
runtime_pm is disabled during system suspend and enabled on resume.
Some client devices trigger I2C transfers before the I2C driver has
resumed completely which causes the I2C transfers to fail. Do
runtime_resume explicitly then so that I2C can work.

http://nvbugs/4765610

Signed-off-by: Akhil R <akhilrajeev@nvidia.com>
Change-Id: Id27cd9979d552216858fa3d3d2b05458a14458c7
(cherry picked from commit 292c376b1ae077a6551ce2b91a03208758ccdf31)
Reviewed-on: https://git-master.nvidia.com/r/c/3rdparty/canonical/linux-noble/+/3193516
Reviewed-by: Petlozu Pravareshwar <petlozup@nvidia.com>
Tested-by: Petlozu Pravareshwar <petlozup@nvidia.com>
Reviewed-by: Laxman Dewangan <ldewangan@nvidia.com>
GVS: buildbot_gerritrpt <buildbot_gerritrpt@nvidia.com>

diff --git a/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-tegra.c b/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-tegra.c
index ce08644f2aac8..03c8359c3f38f 100644
--- a/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-tegra.c
+++ b/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-tegra.c
@@ -339,6 +339,9 @@ static u32 dvc_readl(struct tegra_i2c_dev *i2c_dev, unsigned int reg)
 	return readl_relaxed(i2c_dev->base + reg);
 }
 
+static int tegra_i2c_runtime_resume(struct device *dev);
+static int tegra_i2c_runtime_suspend(struct device *dev);
+
 /*
  * If necessary, i2c_writel() and i2c_readl() will offset the register
  * in order to talk to the I2C block inside the DVC block.
@@ -1514,10 +1517,16 @@ static int tegra_i2c_xfer(struct i2c_adapter *adap, struct i2c_msg msgs[],
 	struct tegra_i2c_dev *i2c_dev = i2c_get_adapdata(adap);
 	int i, ret;
 
-	ret = pm_runtime_get_sync(i2c_dev->dev);
+	if (pm_runtime_enabled(i2c_dev->dev))
+		ret = pm_runtime_get_sync(i2c_dev->dev);
+	else
+		ret = tegra_i2c_runtime_resume(i2c_dev->dev);
+
 	if (ret < 0) {
+		if (pm_runtime_enabled(i2c_dev->dev))
+			pm_runtime_put_noidle(i2c_dev->dev);
+
 		dev_err(i2c_dev->dev, "runtime resume failed %d\n", ret);
-		pm_runtime_put_noidle(i2c_dev->dev);
 		return ret;
 	}
 
@@ -1555,7 +1564,11 @@ static int tegra_i2c_xfer(struct i2c_adapter *adap, struct i2c_msg msgs[],
 	}
 
 	ret = tegra_i2c_mutex_unlock(i2c_dev);
-	pm_runtime_put(i2c_dev->dev);
+
+	if (pm_runtime_enabled(i2c_dev->dev))
+		pm_runtime_put(i2c_dev->dev);
+	else
+		tegra_i2c_runtime_suspend(i2c_dev->dev);
 
 	return ret ?: i;
 }
-- 
